>>> flash 2>&1
flash 2>&1; echo __END_ca0c6fc9__
Usage:
  flash -n                     - Get ap name
  flash -h                     - Get ap head
  flash -p                     - Get ap password	0x56
  flash -a                     - Get ap channel	0x76
  flash -y                     - Get only usb		0xba
  flash -u                     - Get uart status
  flash -x                     - Set ap params, ApName, ApHead, ApPass, Uart null
  flash -m                     - Get Mac address
  flash -r <offset> -c <count> - read <count> bytes from <offset>
  flash -s <offset> -c <count> - read <count> bytes from <offset>
  flash -w <offset> -o <value> - write <offset> with <value>
  flash -f <start> -l <end>    - erase from <start> to <end>
Note:
  <count> is decimal, the other parameters are hexadecimal
__END_ca0c6fc9__
